---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Cove Privacy"
  description="Privacy notes for Cove, the local media organizer, and the public docs site."
  imagePath="/images/screenshots/roles-permission-editor.png"
>
  <section class="marketing-section">
    <div class="marketing-section-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow-small">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="page-heading">Cove is designed to keep library data on your own system</h1>
      <p class="page-copy">
        By default, Cove runs where you install it and does not send library data or telemetry anywhere. External traffic happens only when you deliberately enable features that depend on outside providers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="marketing-section">
    <div class="marketing-section-inner info-grid">
      <article class="info-card">
        <h3>Cove app</h3>
        <p>No telemetry. Your media records, generated assets, user accounts, permissions, and metadata history remain on the system running Cove.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="info-card">
        <h3>External providers</h3>
        <p>Metadata servers, scrapers, downloaders, AI-related tools, and other integrations contact outside services only when you configure and use them.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="info-card">
        <h3>This docs site</h3>
        <p>The public website is a static site and does not add first-party analytics by default. If that changes later, the privacy text should be updated to match.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
